{"custom_id":"s-ap_calculus_ab-m01-k0","ok":true,"model":"claude-opus-5-5","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs4o5FBnwfyw2xbXKKNU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"**Answer: (B) 7.021**\n\n1. By the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus, G′(x) = 5 − x·e^(x/3).\n2. Set G′(x) = 0, so x·e^(x/3) = 5. Solving numerically gives x = c ≈ 2.313.\n   - G′ > 0 for x < c, so G is increasing there.\n   - G′ < 0 for x > c, so G is decreasing there.\n   - So G has its maximum at x = c.\n3. Integration by parts gives ∫ t·e^(t/3) dt = 3t·e^(t/3) − 9e^(t/3).\n4. At x = c, e^(c/3) = 5/c. Substituting this:\n   ∫₀^c t·e^(t/3) dt = (15 − 45/c) − (−9) = 24 − 45/c ≈ 4.545\n5. G(c) = 5c − (24 − 45/c) ≈ 11.565 − 4.545 ≈ 7.02.\n6. Check the endpoints:\n   - G(0) = 0\n   - G(4) = 20 − (3e^(4/3) + 9) ≈ −0.381. This value is distractor (D).\n\nThe maximum value of G on [0, 4] is 7.021. The item is not ambiguous or flawed."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01T2pQBHJ2dwBw2vEwfCrn8V","name":"submit_solution","input":{"answers":[{"item":"1","brief_reasoning":"G'=5-xe^{x/3}=0 at x≈2.313; G there = 5c-(24-45/c)≈7.02; endpoints G(0)=0, G(4)≈-0.381.","ambiguous_or_flawed":false,"choice_index":1,"final_answer":"7.021"}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":238,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":568,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":948,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":346},"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null},"usage":{"input_tokens":238,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":568,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":948,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":346},"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"